"Lone rays of moonlight piercing through the dense vegetation, give way to a narrow path through the thicket.
Step by step you trudge through the cold and wet mud engulfing the ground, until finally, you see it.
A wooden log cabin, with dimly flickering light pulsing from within, standing on a flat patch of ground.
It is said that a man, who can make all your troubles go away, resides in this swamp..
you didn't believe the legends, and yet here you are.. In a final act of desperation you chose to look for this man.
With a big step, you find purchase on the cabins front porch,
shaking off the mud and the vegetation clinging to your boots. There is one lone window on the side of the cabin
but it is much too foggy to see through. You notice the front door is slightly open and you decide to enter..
The old wooden door slowly creeks open. As you step foot inside the cabin, the smell of tabacco rushes up your nostrils.
You also notice a table and two chairs, one of which, a man with a cowboy hat resides on.
You approach the vacant chair and carefully sit down. On the table stands a bottle of whiskey, a packet of cigars,
playing chips and a deck of cards. "Are you here to make your dreams come true?"
the man says, in a guttural, deep voice. You nod.
"good.." he replies, as he slowly lifts his head. You notice an abnormally wide mouth holding a lit cigar.
his smile begins to widen, almost engulfing his entire face. "It's time to gamble, boy.."